[Event "Evans Gambit Accepted"]

{In the Italian, 4.b4 sacrifices a pawn to gain time for c3 and d4. Kasparov and Morphy both used it.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
2... Nc6 {Defends. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
3. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4f7] Aims at f7. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
3... Bc5 {The Giuoco Piano. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
4. b4 {[%cal Gb4c5] The Evans Gambit: decoys the bishop to win time.}
4... Bxb4 {Accepts. The bishop on b4 eyes the pawn on d2.}
5. c3 {[%cal Gc3b4] Gains a tempo on the bishop and prepares d4.}
5... Ba5 {The main line, keeping the bishop on the diagonal.}
 (5... Bc5 {Back to c5. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
6. d4 {[%cal Gd4c5] Centre with tempo. The pawn on d4 eyes the bishop on c5 and the pawn on e5.}
6... exd4 {Takes. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c3.}
7. cxd4 {Recaptures; a big centre. The pawn on d4 eyes the bishop on c5 and controls e5.}
7... Bb4+ {Check. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
8. Bd2 {Blocks and offers a trade. The bishop on d2 eyes the bishop on b4.}
)
6. d4 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4] The point: a big centre and fast development.}
6... exd4 {Takes. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c3.}
 (6... d6 {Holds e5.}
7. Qb3 {[%cal Gb3f7] Hits f7. The queen on b3 eyes the pawn on b7.}
7... Qd7 {Defends f7.}
8. dxe5 {Opens lines. The pawn on e5 eyes the pawn on d6.}
8... dxe5 {Recaptures. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
9. O-O {Castles; Black's king is stuck in the centre for now.}
9... Bb6 {Re-routes the bishop. The bishop on b6 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
10. a4 {[%cal Ga4a5] Harasses the bishop.}
)
7. O-O {Castles, with a lead in development. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Nge7 {Supports a quick ...d5. The knight on e7 controls d5.}
8. cxd4 {Restores the centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
8... d5 {Returns the pawn to free the game. The pawn on d5 eyes the bishop on c4 and the pawn on e4.}
9. exd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c6.}
9... Nxd5 {Recaptures.} *

[Event "Evans Gambit Declined & Lasker"]

{Black can decline with 4...Bb6 or return the pawn with 5...Be7.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nf3 {Attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
2... Nc6 {Defends. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
3. Bc4 {Italian. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
3... Bc5 {Piano. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
4. b4 {Evans Gambit. The pawn on b4 eyes the bishop on c5.}
4... Bb6 {Declines. The bishop on b6 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
 (4... Bxb4 {Accepts. The bishop on b4 eyes the pawn on d2.}
5. c3 {Gains time. The pawn on c3 eyes the bishop on b4 and controls d4.}
5... Be7 {The safe retreat.}
6. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on e5.}
6... Na5 {Hits the c4-bishop. The knight on a5 eyes the bishop on c4.}
7. Nxe5 {[%cal Ge5f7] White takes e5 with threats on f7. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on d7 and the pawn on f7.}
7... Nxc4 {Takes the bishop. The knight on c4 eyes the knight on e5.}
8. Nxc4 {Recaptures. The knight on c4 controls e5.}
8... d5 {Black returns the pawn to develop. The pawn on d5 eyes the knight on c4 and the pawn on e4.}
9. exd5 {Takes.}
9... Qxd5 {Recaptures. The queen on d5 eyes the knight on c4 and the pawn on d4 and controls e4 and e5.}
10. Ne3 {[%cal Ge3d5] Hits the queen. The knight on e3 eyes the queen on d5.}
)
5. a4 {[%cal Ga4a5] Gains queenside space and threatens a5.}
5... a6 {Makes room for the bishop on a7.}
6. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5.} *
